Z||000009||stimpy||09-01-2000||08:34 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Homicidal:<BR><B><BR>Seriously, that's the only reason my 4 Banger can kill some of the 6 Cylinder Civics and other in my area.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>??????????????????????????????????<BR>Six cylinder Civics? Is that anything like a Lexus GT250, or is it more like a twin turbo Fiero?<P>------------------<BR>Loud Pipes Save Lives!      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/stimpy_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000010||mshill||09-02-2000||12:14 PM||||I have a 93 Taurus with the 3.8L V6.  I have to say that when the engine was fresh (back in 95) it was fairly strong and I doubt my fresh 86SE V6 4sp could have beat it back then, but that engine got tired fast.  Just 65K miles on it and it is a real pig now.  Before I rebuilt my 2.8L (had 180K miles, busted exhaust manifolds... the works) the 86SE could blow it away.  I have never been impressed with the Ford V6 engines.  The Chevy V6 on the otherhand seems to be a real work of art.  I have the 4.3L V6 in both my Safari van and my boat, and of course the 2.8L V6 in both my Fieros.  They are all so easy to work on.||||reg||1
Z||000011||86SE||09-03-2000||03:05 AM||||I love my 2.8, its makes me sad that I will get rid of it soon, just the engine. It runs strong with 89,000 and driven hard all its life!  Solid runner, just smokes a little at start up.<P>------------------<BR>'86 Special Edition,<BR>High-Output V-6 Yellow Fiero<BR>Special Rally Heavy Duty Suspention||||reg||14
